# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PratiBimb — .gitignore
# This is a privacy/security product. Git history is part of the
# threat surface. See SECURITY.md before adding an exception.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets — never commit ──────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*token*.txt
.hf_token
.huggingface/
# Secret-bearing files, named narrowly on purpose. A broad `*secret*` glob also
# swallows our own tooling (scripts/check-secrets.sh) and legitimate source such as
# packages/security/secret-scan.ts -- an ignore rule that hides real source is worse
# than no rule, because the omission is silent.
secrets.json
secrets.yml
secrets.yaml
*.secret
.secrets/

# ── Real user / PII data — never commit ─────────────────────
# Only synthetic fixtures belong in this repository.
**/real-data/
**/user-data/
**/pii/
**/*.pii.*
captures/
screenshots/real/
**/browsing-history*
**/vault-dump*

# ── Model weights and large binaries — reference, don't vendor ──
*.onnx
*.onnx_data
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.tflite
models/
!models/**/*.md
!models/**/*.json

# ONNX Runtime Web runtime artifacts are 14-28 MB and are referenced by pinned revision,
# never vendored (W1-S03, W1-S02a-2a-3). Small SYNTHETIC .wasm fixtures - the 41-byte
# add.wasm used by W1-S02a-2a-1 and -2a-4 - remain deliberately tracked, which is why this
# is a targeted rule rather than a blanket `*.wasm`.
ort-wasm-*.wasm
ort-wasm-*.mjs
ort.all.min.js

# Generated by build-extension.js at run time; regenerated from node_modules, not committed.
artifacts/experiments/**/served/
artifacts/experiments/**/ext-chrome/
artifacts/experiments/**/ext-firefox/

# ── Browser profiles produced by spikes ─────────────────────
# Chrome user-data-dirs contain profile state; never commit them.
**/chrome-profile/
**/firefox-profile/
**/.wdm/
**/user-data-dir/

# ── Node ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.output/
.wxt/
*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ── Test / coverage output ──────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/

# ── OS / editor ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json

# ── Scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
tmp/
.tmp/
scratch/
*.local

# ADR-0001 gate harness — generated on every run.
# The extensions under build/ are assembled from the production CSP by
# build-gate-extensions.mjs, and results/ is the raw run output. Neither is a source of
# truth: the evidence that is kept lives under artifacts/adr/ADR-0001/.
tests/browser/gates/build/
tests/browser/gates/results/
artifacts/experiments/W1-B02-invariant-e-observation/harness/regression/guard-result.json
artifacts/datasets/
artifacts/models/

# QG-03 detector runtime harness — assembled on every run from node_modules, the compiled
# packages, and the generated reference fixtures. 45 MB of ORT and a 0.30 MB model that is
# itself gitignored. The evidence that is KEPT is metrics.json, reference-summary.json and
# logs/ — none of which are generated here.
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03-t1-detector-runtime/harness/ext-chrome/
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03-t1-detector-runtime/harness/ext-firefox/
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03-t1-detector-runtime/harness/generated/

# QG-03b preprocessing conformance harness — assembled per run; generated/ holds ~100 MB of
# reference pixel dumps. The evidence that is KEPT is fixtures.json (digests only),
# geometry-comparison.json, metrics.json and logs/.
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03b-letterbox-conformance/harness/ext-chrome/
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03b-letterbox-conformance/harness/ext-firefox/
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03b-letterbox-conformance/harness/generated/

# QG-03b-2 capture-format conformance harness — assembled per run. generated/ holds the
# encoded fixtures and ~180 MB of reference pixel dumps. Kept evidence: fixtures.json
# (digests only), metrics.json and logs/.
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03b2-capture-format-conformance/harness/ext-chrome/
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03b2-capture-format-conformance/harness/ext-firefox/
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03b2-capture-format-conformance/harness/generated/

# QG-03b-2a real-capture harness — assembled per run. generated/ holds the reference
# decode dumps (~338 MB) and ext-chrome/ the assembled extension (~198 MB of ORT plus the
# compiled packages). Both are rebuilt from committed inputs by build-qg03b2a-extension.mjs.
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03b2a-chromium-jpeg-capture/harness/ext-chrome/
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03b2a-chromium-jpeg-capture/harness/generated/
# The SECOND capture of each fixture exists to prove the encoder is deterministic. Its
# evidence is the digest recorded in captured/manifest.json, which is committed; the file
# itself is a byte-for-byte duplicate of the first and is not worth carrying in history.
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03b2a-chromium-jpeg-capture/harness/captured/*.r2.*

# QG-03a production-path robustness harness. generated/ holds the Pillow reference pixel
# dumps and the encoded fixtures; profiles/ the throwaway browser profiles. Both are rebuilt
# by qg03a_reference.py and run-a-browser.mjs. Kept evidence: reference.json (digests only),
# metrics.json and logs/.
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03a-t1-production-robustness/harness/generated/
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03a-t1-production-robustness/harness/profiles/

# QG-03a-B2 real-model harness. generated/ holds the raw ORT output dumps (~6 MB per cell);
# profiles/ holds the throwaway browser profiles. The model itself is already ignored under
# artifacts/models/. Kept evidence: logs/ (every digest), metrics.json.
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03a-B2-real-model-nms/harness/generated/
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03a-B2-real-model-nms/harness/profiles/

# QG-03a-B3-1 MV3 extension harness. ext-chrome/ is assembled per run (ignored above);
# generated/ holds the raw ORT output dumps (~6 MB per cell, per machine) and browser profiles
# live in the OS temp directory. The detections of a DEVELOPMENT run are not evidence, so they
# are not committed either; a workstation-1 run commits logs/workstation-1/detections/.
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03a-B3-1-mv3-extension-backends/harness/generated/
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03a-B3-1-mv3-extension-backends/logs/development-*/detections/
# QG-03a-C3 label/raster generalisation harness. generated/ holds the rendered PNGs, the RGBA
# dumps, the raw ORT outputs and the per-cell manifests - all reproducible from the recipe
# (spec version + seed + the harness). Committed: the records, the harness, logs/ and metrics.json.
artifacts/experiments/W1-QG03a-C3-label-raster-generalisation/harness/generated/

# W-1 detector precision/scale harness. generated/ holds the regenerated dev-split frames,
# the scale-control renders, the Pillow RGBA dumps and the per-cell manifests - about 1.9 GB,
# and all of it reproducible from the recipe: the unchanged tools/dataset/build-dataset.mjs
# at seed 20260910 (hash 4bbc57de), then render-arm-b.mjs and decode-w1-png.py.
artifacts/experiments/W1-detector-precision-scale/harness/generated/

# Track B geometry/appearance harness. generated/ holds 480 rendered frames, their RGBA dumps
# and the per-cell manifests - reproducible from render-trackb.mjs, apply-appearance.py and
# decode-trackb.py at the recorded dataset and model identities.
artifacts/experiments/W1-TrackB-geometry-appearance/harness/generated/


# MVP-0 harness. The captured frame is locally generated and small enough to commit as
# demo evidence; the decoded RGBA is a 3 MB intermediate reproducible from it.
artifacts/experiments/MVP-0-dom-sufficiency/logs/*.rgba
